{% comment %}
  Does this teacher also sell work here? Outputs the URL and the title of her
  artist collection, or nothing at all.

  {% render %} cannot hand variables back to its caller, so this echoes one
  string — "<url>|<title>" — exactly the way snippets/rb-teacher-handle.liquid
  echoes a handle. Capture it and split it in the caller:

    {%- capture rb_ac -%}
      {%- render 'rb-artist-collection', teacher_name: instr, product: product -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign rb_ac = rb_ac | strip
      assign rb_artist_url = ''
      assign rb_artist_name = ''
      if rb_ac != blank
        assign rb_artist_url = rb_ac | split: '|' | first
        assign rb_artist_name = rb_ac | split: '|' | last
      endif
    -%}

  Why it exists: /pages/the-team now sends a visitor straight to the class, so
  the class page's "See Teachers Page" button pointed back at a collection they
  had already been through. A teacher who also exhibits has somewhere better to
  send them — her own work.

  Resolution, in order:

    1. booking.artist_collection on the product. A handle typed against the
       class always wins; nothing below can overrule it.
    2. the catalogue, matched on the VENDOR of the collection's first product.
       Vendor rather than handle because the handles are not trustworthy:
       Careshia's teacher collection is "careshia-esperanza" and her artist one
       is "careisha-esperanza" — one letter apart, and guessing lands on the
       wrong page.
    3. nothing, which is the answer for most teachers.

  Two departures from the obvious version of pass 2, both forced by the live
  catalogue (checked 2026-09-18):

  * The collection's TITLE narrows the field before any product is read. Every
    artist collection here is titled with the artist's name, so this is both a
    fair filter and the cheap one: of 39 collections, at most two ever load a
    product. Without it every non-empty collection would.

  * Name matching falls back to the SURNAME, as rb-teacher-handle already does,
    because the catalogue spells people differently in different places. The
    class credits "Zara Farinha"; her work is filed under "Zara-Leigh Farinha".
    Whole-string matching alone would lose her.

  A collection whose first product is a Class is a teacher collection, not an
  artist one, and is skipped — that is what keeps a teacher who does not
  exhibit (Susan, Janice, Petronella, Chloe, Shabana) resolving to nothing.
  The largest qualifying collection wins, so a stray one-off never beats the
  real body of work.

  The title also has to survive being joined with "|", which is why no
  collection title here may contain that character.

  Accepts: teacher_name (string), product (optional, for the override).
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign ac_name = teacher_name | strip
  assign ac_out = ''

  comment
    1. The manual override. Read off the product so one class can be pinned to
       a collection this snippet would never have found.
  endcomment
  assign ac_manual = product.metafields.booking.artist_collection | strip
  if ac_manual != blank
    assign ac_col = collections[ac_manual]
    comment
      collections[unknown] is nil, and nil.all_products_count > 0 is a render
      error rather than a false — hence the nested test on the handle first.
      Liquid evaluates `and` right to left, so a one-line guard would not have
      protected the comparison.
    endcomment
    if ac_col.handle != blank
      assign ac_out = ac_col.url | append: '|' | append: ac_col.title
    endif
  endif

  comment
    2. Find it. ac_best holds the size of the best match so far, so the biggest
       qualifying collection is the one that survives the loop.
  endcomment
  if ac_out == blank and ac_name != blank
    assign ac_low = ac_name | downcase | strip
    assign ac_surname = ac_low | split: ' ' | last
    assign ac_best = 0

    for c in collections limit: 250
      if c.all_products_count == 0
        continue
      endif

      assign ac_title = c.title | downcase | strip
      assign ac_title_hit = false
      if ac_title == ac_low
        assign ac_title_hit = true
      elsif ac_surname != blank and ac_title contains ac_surname
        assign ac_title_hit = true
      endif
      unless ac_title_hit
        continue
      endunless

      comment
        The only product read anywhere in this snippet.
      endcomment
      assign ac_first = c.products.first
      if ac_first.type == 'Class'
        continue
      endif

      assign ac_vendor = ac_first.vendor | downcase | strip
      assign ac_vendor_hit = false
      if ac_vendor == ac_low
        assign ac_vendor_hit = true
      elsif ac_surname != blank and ac_vendor != blank and ac_vendor contains ac_surname
        assign ac_vendor_hit = true
      endif

      if ac_vendor_hit
        if c.all_products_count > ac_best
          assign ac_best = c.all_products_count
          assign ac_out = c.url | append: '|' | append: c.title
        endif
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  echo ac_out
-%}
